      "Using web search before checking relevant local documentation indexes."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What does this skill help with?",
        "answer": "It helps AI assistants navigate local ai-docs indexes and load focused documentation for development tasks."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does it search the web?",
        "answer": "No. It recommends checking local documentation first and using web search only when local docs are insufficient."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which documentation formats does it describe?",
        "answer": "It focuses on hierarchical ai-docs indexes, TOON page summaries, and optional full-context markdown files."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can it update documentation files?",
        "answer": "No. The skill provides navigation guidance and does not edit documentation or generate indexes."
      },
      {
        "question": "When should full-context files be loaded?",
        "answer": "Use them for major migrations, comprehensive tutorials, or broad initial learning, not quick lookups."
      },
